If format is not specified the default "%a %b %d %H:%M:%S %Y" value is used.


time(), time_ns()

Returns the current Unix time stamp in UTC as a float. Not all systems support a higher resolution that one second,so the fractional part isn't necessarily reliable.
The time_ns variant differs from time in such a way that the result isn't returned as a float in seconds, but as an integer in nanoseconds.


