>>> gifts
datetime.datetime(1989, 12, 25, 18, 30)

A datetime instance has an attribute for each of these parameters. For example:

>>> gifts.minute
30
>>> gifts.month
12


now()

The now() method creates a datetime instance that stores the current local time. 

>>> datetime.datetime.now()
datetime.datetime (2026, 11, 17, 12, 10, 1, 25484)

fromtimestamp(timestamp)

The fromtimestamp method creates a datetime.datetime instance that represents the same time as the Unix time stamp passed for timestamp in the system's local time:

>>> datetime.datetime.fromtimestamp(0)
datetime.datetime (1970, 1, 1, 1, 0)


combine(date,time) 
The combine method creates a datetime.datetime object that stems from the combination of date and time. The date parameter must contain a datetime.date instance, and time parameter must refer to a datetime.time object.

strptime(date_string,format)
The strptime method interprets the string passed as the date_string parameter as time information according to the format description from format and returns a corresponding datetime object. 

